From e261a5cf82b6bab77105ea9488e5617e92a0b52f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:34:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] widescreen auto-UI: classify HUD by vertex provenance
 (auto_ui_provenance)

New opt-in [widescreen] auto_ui_provenance for the projection-and-stretch
path. Instead of ordering-table rank, the auto-UI prepass asks the PGXP
dataflow shadow (armed for this) whether each vertex word was produced by a
GTE projection:

- A primitive with a projected vertex is world geometry and never squashed
  as HUD, however axis-aligned or close to the HUD it is.
- Every other screen-space primitive is a HUD candidate at any rank,
  including single GP0 lines (box outlines) and large panels, and is
  grouped and anchored in screen space (packet + draw offset - area).
- 2D drawn behind the scene (below the 10th percentile of the world's ranks)
  is a backdrop; a 2D line below the 90th percentile is a scene effect.
- A run that overlaps a picture the game uploaded into the frame buffer keeps
  the picture's stretched layout.
- A projected model inside a small admitted HUD box moves with the box.

Fixes Action Man: Mission Xtreme's language-screen flag cells being squashed
as HUD (black flickering holes) and HUD box outlines, 3D icons and backing
panels coming apart from their boxes. Rank-based classification is unchanged
when the option is off. New test: ws_auto_ui_provenance_exec_test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
